[{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"37a26d069b301c2ff3d6aaafeb810c1eb3c4e818810ebb58384748de3c997ed1","event_uuid":"dba5b145-35cd-465e-ab20-19e59dac3327","position":{"commit_sha":"03e0fb3738e96c67d87e77b827a1eecbf3cffeec","position":"1787452524300050001-dba5b145-35cd-465e-ab20-19e59dac3327"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"DESIGN DECISION (operator-ratified, grounded in OSS research): adopt option 2 from the ticket — DROP timeout_func_only from [tool.pytest.ini_options] so it reverts to pytest-timeout's upstream default (False), making the per-test 300 s budget cover fixture setup and teardown. Precedent: pytest-timeout's own default for func_only is False, and its README positions func_only as a last-resort workaround ('firstly make the timeouts larger'); pandas, numpy, and scikit-learn set no timeout_func_only. If dropping the key makes any slow-fixture test trip the budget, the remedy is to RAISE that test's timeout via @pytest.mark.timeout(N) (the README-sanctioned remedy), never to restore func_only. REJECTED: option 1 session_timeout — it is cooperative (checked between tests), cannot stop a hanging test, and the README says it complements per-test timeouts, never substitutes. REJECTED: option 3 targeted per-fixture guards — no ecosystem precedent. The 300 s budget already DWARFS the slowest legitimate call time (29.93 s), so charging fixture time to the first requesting test carries low trip risk.","timestamp":1787437741986557001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 2141 (commit 121a6bd5e8d): dropped timeout_func_only from [tool.pytest.ini_options] (reverts to upstream default False; budget now covers setup+call+teardown); rewrote the ini comment citing this ticket and 89d5-61da-b621-47f8; test_timeout_budget.py reworked — config arm asserts the key's ABSENCE, new out-of-process negative arms prove a hanging fixture SETUP and a hanging TEARDOWN are expired and named by the ini alone, and a remedy arm proves a plain @pytest.mark.timeout(N) absorbs legitimately slow fixture time; comment-only updates in test_timeout_budget_headroom.py, _build-and-test.yml, docs/local-dev-env.md. RED-first verified: config arm failed against the old ini before the key removal. Local gates green: make lint (incl. complexity ratchet), make typecheck, targeted suites (34 passed: timeout_budget, headroom, ci_workflow_parity). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1787449383165156001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CLOSE EVIDENCE: Gerrit change 2141 MERGED to main as aa0668b0ee3 (LLM-Review +1 from the rebar review bot, Verified +1 from CI run 32611006643, zero unresolved comments; submitted 2026-08-23 02:27 UTC). All ACs verified: (1) timeout_func_only removed from [tool.pytest.ini_options] — config arm test_the_configured_budget_is_the_measured_one asserts the key's ABSENCE and fails on reappearance; (2) hanging SETUP and TEARDOWN are bounded and named — out-of-process arms test_a_hanging_fixture_setup_is_bounded_by_the_ini and test_a_hanging_teardown_is_bounded_by_the_ini assert a pytest-timeout Timeout in the nested run (RED-first: config arm failed against the old ini before the removal); (3) slow-fixture remedy proven — test_a_marker_covers_legitimately_slow_fixture_time shows a plain @pytest.mark.timeout(N) absorbs fixture time past a tighter ini budget; (4) pyproject ini comment cites 797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5 and 89d5-61da-b621-47f8. Local gates were green pre-push (make lint incl. complexity ratchet, make typecheck, 34 targeted tests) and the Verified run confirms the full suite passes with fixture time charged to tests — no slow-fixture test tripped the 300 s budget. Closing as regression caused-by bold-abeyant-indri (73b8-2d79-3046-44ce), whose commit 6a5c88027c5 introduced timeout_func_only=true and thereby removed the fixture-phase coverage the 89d5 guard had established.","timestamp":1787452404460588001}],"created_at":1787419324254223001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8a8f79dd-4298-49ff-88e7-b1bebb0431ef","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3fa7-94ba-42aa-4623"},{"link_uuid":"6e474b78-6095-4656-98ea-925d89de430d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"89d5-61da-b621-47f8"},{"link_uuid":"d837642b-9b79-46d5-9238-b4394dcdb3d2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2ced-55f3-a36d-4073"},{"link_uuid":"dba5b145-35cd-465e-ab20-19e59dac3327","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8908-043d-c697-4493"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`pyproject.toml` `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` carries `timeout_func_only = true` (added by story\n`bold-abeyant-indri`, commit `6a5c88027c5`, at `pyproject.toml:664`). pytest-timeout documents\nthat key as deferring the timeout evaluation to only the test function body, ignoring fixture\ntime — so fixture SETUP and TEARDOWN are unguarded by the per-test hang budget. That is the\nexact phase the guard was originally built for: bug `89d5-61da-b621-47f8` was filed because a\n`with TestClient(app)` teardown awaited `queue.join()` under a 1200 s drain and burned the full\n60-minute job cap. The guard that landed then (`--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread`, no\n`func_only`) covered all phases; the current ini does not.\n\n## Approach\n\nDrop the `timeout_func_only = true` line from `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` so the key reverts to\npytest-timeout's upstream default (`False`) and the 300 s budget covers fixture setup and\nteardown again. This is the ecosystem-standard shape: pytest-timeout's own default for\n`func_only` is `False` and its README positions `func_only` as a last-resort workaround\n(\"firstly make the timeouts larger\"); pandas, numpy, and scikit-learn configure no\n`timeout_func_only`. The 300 s budget is already sized to DWARF the slowest legitimate test\n(measured worst `call` 29.93 s, pinned in `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py`), so\ncharging fixture time to the first requesting test carries low trip risk. Default: if CI shows\nany slow-fixture test tripping the budget after this lands, RAISE that test's own timeout with\n`@pytest.mark.timeout(N)` (the README-sanctioned remedy) rather than restoring `func_only`.\nNot `session_timeout`: it is cooperative — evaluated between tests — so it cannot stop a\nhanging test. The rewritten ini comment cites this ticket and `89d5-61da-b621-47f8`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `pyproject.toml` — remove `timeout_func_only = true`; rewrite the budget comment block to\n  explain full-phase coverage, citing `797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5` and `89d5-61da-b621-47f8`.\n- `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` — update the config assertion\n  (`test_the_configured_budget_is_the_measured_one`) to require the key's ABSENCE; add the two\n  out-of-process arms described under Testing. Rework the EXISTING material for coherence with\n  the new policy: the module docstring (currently framing the positive arm around\n  `func_only=True`) is rewritten to describe full-phase coverage and the plain-marker remedy;\n  the existing positive arm `test_a_marked_test_may_outrun_the_ini_budget` keeps its purpose\n  (marker beats ini) but its generated project drops `timeout_func_only = true` and its\n  generated marker becomes `@pytest.mark.timeout(120)` (no `func_only`); the existing negative\n  arm's generated ini likewise drops the key; the in-repo `@pytest.mark.timeout(180,\n  func_only=True)` guards on the arm functions themselves become `@pytest.mark.timeout(180)`.\n- `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py` — comment-only: reword the sentence that\n  explains the measured worst times in terms of `timeout_func_only = true`.\n- `docs/local-dev-env.md` — update the per-test hang budget section (it currently documents\n  `timeout_func_only = true` and the body-only semantics), including its example override\n  snippet, which shows `@pytest.mark.timeout(90, func_only=True)`.\n- `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` — comment-only: the default-suite step's comment\n  (lines 660–662) prescribes `@pytest.mark.timeout(N, func_only=True)` for legitimately\n  longer tests; reword it to the plain `@pytest.mark.timeout(N)` remedy so it does not\n  contradict the new full-phase policy. No `run:` command changes.\n\n## Testing\n\nBoth new arms run out-of-process against a generated project via the shared\n`run_nested_pytest` helper (the same style as the existing negative arm in\n`tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py`, per story 25b4's single-launch-site guard), each with a\ndeliberately tiny budget so they cost seconds:\n\n- Negative arm (hang coverage): a generated project mirrors this repo's ini keys (timeout=2,\n  `timeout_method = \"thread\"`, no `func_only`) and contains a test whose FIXTURE SETUP sleeps\n  past the budget, and a second project whose TEARDOWN sleeps past it; both nested runs must\n  fail with a pytest-timeout `Timeout` naming the test, not hang.\n- Positive arm (the sanctioned remedy): in a generated project with `timeout = 2` and a shared\n  fixture that sleeps past that budget, a test carrying `@pytest.mark.timeout(30)` passes —\n  proving a legitimately slow-fixture test has a supported per-test escape, so dropping\n  `func_only` does not force fixture cost onto an unraisable budget.\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the targeted suites\n(`pytest tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py`) run\ngreen before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` no longer sets `timeout_func_only`; checked by the updated\n      config assertion in `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` failing if the key reappears.\n- [x] A test whose SETUP or TEARDOWN hangs is bounded and names itself rather than running to\n      the job cap; demonstrated by the out-of-process nested-pytest negative arms (fixture-\n      setup hang and teardown hang) asserting a `Timeout` failure in the nested run.\n- [x] A legitimately slow shared fixture does not strand its test without recourse: the\n      positive arm proves `@pytest.mark.timeout(N)` on the test covers fixture time and passes\n      under a tighter ini budget.\n- [x] The chosen configuration is recorded in `pyproject.toml` with a comment citing this\n      ticket (`797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5`) and `89d5-61da-b621-47f8`; checked by reading the ini\n      comment block in the landed change.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"remove timeout_func_only = true; rewrite the hang-budget comment citing 797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5 and 89d5-61da-b621-47f8"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py","reason":"assert the key is absent; rework docstring and existing arms off func_only; add fixture-setup/teardown hang negative arms and the marker-remedy positive arm"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py","reason":"comment-only reword of the func_only sentence"},{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"update the per-test hang budget section and its func_only example snippet"},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"comment-only: reword the func_only override prescription at lines 660-662 to the plain marker remedy"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2ced-55f3-a36d-4073"],["relates_to","8908-043d-c697-4493"],["relates_to","89d5-61da-b621-47f8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"46d5fb64-4db8-48b5-94fb-3fb330db3558","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"timeout_func_only leaves fixture setup/teardown hangs unguarded","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4bbbd877-8432-4713-906c-db0a191b465c","dabaa18c-6b64-4f09-a86c-9bb56da420d3","4e421d7b-6153-457a-98d0-a2c872079ae9","49d532eb-6843-435b-a4dd-c5e2bb0eb629","c9f8c640-8541-49c8-80e4-24c422a52f17","d837642b-9b79-46d5-9238-b4394dcdb3d2","1fb5b01d-b62f-4152-ad55-f9e5dbbdf2ca","46d5fb64-4db8-48b5-94fb-3fb330db3558","56041799-84a3-4eb1-a5ee-5f22e3c0df20","cdd437cd-4190-4c03-80a7-50a72002285f","069ddb83-54f5-4a51-9f48-3ce4653dd9fd","5fe298db-6bcb-436a-b68e-8f01d9c8fe05","dba5b145-35cd-465e-ab20-19e59dac3327"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787454371289876001,"uuid":"66680571-89a1-4ff6-acc6-670fca4a387d"}